export default {"format":"cadcraft-help","version":1,"app":"cadcraft","addon":"pid","name":"P&ID","sections":{"start":"Getting started","tasks":"Walkthroughs","switching":"Coming from other software","reference":"Reference","trouble":"Troubleshooting and limits"},"topics":[{"slug":"pid-start","scope":"addon:pid","title":"P&ID: getting started","summary":"What the P&ID add-on does in CadCraft, how to switch it on, and how a diagram is kept in an ordinary DWG or DXF file.","section":"start","order":1,"keywords":["p&id","pid","process","instrumentation","diagram","piping and instrumentation","tag","line number","instrument","equipment","line list","add-on"],"headings":[{"id":"what-it-is","text":"What it is","level":2},{"id":"your-first-diagram","text":"Your first diagram","level":2},{"id":"files-open-anywhere","text":"Files open anywhere","level":2},{"id":"units","text":"Units","level":2}],"html":"\u003Ch2 id=\"what-it-is\"\u003EWhat it is\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EP&amp;ID is an add-on for CadCraft that comes with it and is free. It draws process and instrumentation diagrams: equipment, valves, instruments and the lines between them, with a tag on each item and a number on each line. From the finished drawing it makes the lists a diagram is read for (line list, equipment list, instrument index, valve list) and checks the drawing for the mistakes that are easy to miss.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EIt is off until you switch it on: \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESettings\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EGeneral\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EAdd-ons\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EP&amp;ID\u003C/span\u003E. Its tools are in the \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EP&amp;ID\u003C/span\u003E section of the right panel, as commands (below), and, when you ask for it in \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESettings\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ECadCraft\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EP&amp;ID\u003C/span\u003E, as a group at the end of the toolbar.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EA drafting aid, not an engineering approval.\u003C/strong\u003E The symbols are drawn by CadCraft after the common ideas of the standards named in &quot;P&amp;ID: symbols, tags and equipment&quot;; the line numbers, tags and checks follow the usual habits of these diagrams, not any company&#039;s or standard&#039;s rules. A person who is responsible for the plant still decides what the diagram has to say.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"your-first-diagram\"\u003EYour first diagram\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EType \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDSYMBOL\u003C/code\u003E, type \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ES\u003C/span\u003E to choose a symbol (first its kind, then the symbol), and click where it goes. Equipment asks for its tag; the next free one is offered (\u003Ccode\u003EP-101\u003C/code\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003ET-101\u003C/code\u003E).\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EType \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDLINE\u003C/code\u003E, type \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EV\u003C/span\u003E, \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EZ\u003C/span\u003E and \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EP\u003C/span\u003E for the service, size and spec (\u003Ccode\u003EPW\u003C/code\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003E2&quot;\u003C/code\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003EA1A\u003C/code\u003E), and click the corners of a process line. Start and finish on a nozzle: the click lands on it.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPut a valve on the line: \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDSYMBOL\u003C/code\u003E, a valve, and click on the line. The line is cut either side of the valve.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPlace an instrument, type its letters (\u003Ccode\u003EFIC\u003C/code\u003E) and it takes the next loop number (\u003Ccode\u003EFIC-101\u003C/code\u003E). Draw a signal line to it: \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDLINE\u003C/code\u003E, \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EY\u003C/span\u003E for a signal style.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EType \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDCHECK\u003C/code\u003E and go to each finding. Type \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDLIST\u003C/code\u003E and click where a list goes on the sheet.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ol\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"files-open-anywhere\"\u003EFiles open anywhere\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA symbol, a line and a list on the sheet are each saved as a block reference with its drawing inside, and its data kept with it under the application name \u003Ccode\u003ECC_PID\u003C/code\u003E. A diagram saved as DWG or DXF opens in any CAD program as drawn, and in CadCraft without the add-on with nothing lost.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EConnections are never stored: CadCraft works them out from where things touch, so moving a pump with \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EMOVE\u003C/code\u003E keeps the diagram true.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"units\"\u003EUnits\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ESymbols are 4 in (100 mm in a metric drawing) by default; change it in \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESettings\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ECadCraft\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EP&amp;ID\u003C/span\u003E. Sizes in line numbers are text: type what your drawings say (\u003Ccode\u003E2&quot;\u003C/code\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003EDN50\u003C/code\u003E).\u003C/p\u003E","text":"What it is P&ID is an add-on for CadCraft that comes with it and is free. It draws process and instrumentation diagrams: equipment, valves, instruments and the lines between them, with a tag on each item and a number on each line. From the finished drawing it makes the lists a diagram is read for (line list, equipment list, instrument index, valve list) and checks the drawing for the mistakes that are easy to miss. It is off until you switch it on: Settings › General › Add-ons › P&ID. Its tools are in the P&ID section of the right panel, as commands (below), and, when you ask for it in Settings › CadCraft › P&ID, as a group at the end of the toolbar. A drafting aid, not an engineering approval. The symbols are drawn by CadCraft after the common ideas of the standards named in \"P&ID: symbols, tags and equipment\"; the line numbers, tags and checks follow the usual habits of these diagrams, not any company's or standard's rules. A person who is responsible for the plant still decides what the diagram has to say. Your first diagram Type PIDSYMBOL, type S to choose a symbol (first its kind, then the symbol), and click where it goes. Equipment asks for its tag; the next free one is offered (P-101, T-101). Type PIDLINE, type V, Z and P for the service, size and spec (PW, 2\", A1A), and click the corners of a process line. Start and finish on a nozzle: the click lands on it. Put a valve on the line: PIDSYMBOL, a valve, and click on the line. The line is cut either side of the valve. Place an instrument, type its letters (FIC) and it takes the next loop number (FIC-101). Draw a signal line to it: PIDLINE, Y for a signal style. Type PIDCHECK and go to each finding. Type PIDLIST and click where a list goes on the sheet. Files open anywhere A symbol, a line and a list on the sheet are each saved as a block reference with its drawing inside, and its data kept with it under the application name CC_PID. A diagram saved as DWG or DXF opens in any CAD program as drawn, and in CadCraft without the add-on with nothing lost. Connections are never stored: CadCraft works them out from where things touch, so moving a pump with MOVE keeps the diagram true. Units Symbols are 4 in (100 mm in a metric drawing) by default; change it in Settings › CadCraft › P&ID. Sizes in line numbers are text: type what your drawings say (2\", DN50)."},{"slug":"pid-symbols","scope":"addon:pid","title":"P&ID: symbols, tags and equipment","summary":"The symbol library and the standards it follows, placing symbols, valves with actuators, in-line items that cut a line, and tags.","section":"tasks","order":10,"keywords":["symbol","valve","gate","globe","ball","check","butterfly","actuator","pump","vessel","tank","exchanger","instrument","balloon","tag","ISA","ISO","nozzle","connection"],"headings":[{"id":"the-library","text":"The library","level":2},{"id":"placing-symbols","text":"Placing symbols","level":2},{"id":"tags","text":"Tags","level":2}],"html":"\u003Ch2 id=\"the-library\"\u003EThe library\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDSYMBOL\u003C/code\u003E places any of 52 symbols in five kinds, and a valve can carry any of five actuators.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"ht-wrap\"\u003E\u003Ctable class=\"ht\"\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003EKind\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003ESymbols\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003EStandard idea it follows\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EValves\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Egate, globe, ball, check, butterfly, plug, needle, diaphragm, angle, three-way, pressure relief, rupture disc\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EISO 10628 (symbols for chemical and process engineering diagrams)\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EActuators\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ediaphragm, motor, solenoid, piston, hand operated\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EISO 10628\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EEquipment\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Evertical and horizontal vessel, storage tank, sphere, column, reactor, shell and tube and plate exchanger, air cooler, fired heater, centrifugal and positive displacement pump, compressor, fan, filter, agitator\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EISO 10628\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EInstruments\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eballoons: field, main panel, local panel, shared display, computer function, programmable logic controller\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EISA-5.1 (instrument identification: the balloon and where it is mounted)\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EIn-line items\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ereducer, cap, flange, blind flange, spectacle blind, union, orifice plate, strainer, sight glass, expansion joint, flame arrestor, specification break\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EISO 10628; orifice plate ISA-5.1; specification break ISO 14617\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EConnectors and line ends\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eoff-page connector (to, from), flow arrow, vent, drain, tie-in point\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EISO 14617 (symbols for diagrams), ISO 10628\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/tbody\u003E\u003C/table\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EEvery shape is drawn by CadCraft and dedicated to the public domain (CC0 1.0): use them anywhere. The standards give the idea of a shape (a bow tie for a valve, a circle for a pump, a circle for an instrument); no vendor&#039;s symbol library and no standard&#039;s own artwork was copied or traced. The tables of letters and shapes in a standard are the standard&#039;s: for a drawing that has to follow one, check it against the standard itself.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"placing-symbols\"\u003EPlacing symbols\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EType \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDSYMBOL\u003C/code\u003E. \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ES\u003C/span\u003E chooses the symbol (its kind first), \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EA\u003C/span\u003E turns the next symbols, and for a valve \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ET\u003C/span\u003E chooses its actuator. Click to place; Enter ends.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ENozzles.\u003C/strong\u003E Equipment, valves and instruments have connection points (a pump&#039;s suction and discharge, a vessel&#039;s top, bottom and sides). A click near a line end or another symbol&#039;s connection puts the new symbol&#039;s nearest connection exactly there.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EIn-line items cut the line.\u003C/strong\u003E A valve, reducer, strainer or other in-line symbol clicked on a process line is turned along the line and cuts it: two pieces, each ending on the symbol. They keep the line number; one piece writes it. \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EUNDO\u003C/code\u003E puts the line back whole.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EValves with actuators\u003C/strong\u003E have one more connection, on top of the actuator, where a signal line ends. A check valve, relief valve and rupture disc take no actuator.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"tags\"\u003ETags\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EEquipment, instruments and pressure relief devices need a tag; the checks say so when one is missing.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EEquipment\u003C/strong\u003E is offered the next free tag with a prefix by kind (\u003Ccode\u003EP-101\u003C/code\u003E pumps, \u003Ccode\u003ET-101\u003C/code\u003E tanks and spheres, \u003Ccode\u003EV-101\u003C/code\u003E vessels, \u003Ccode\u003EE-101\u003C/code\u003E exchangers, \u003Ccode\u003EC-101\u003C/code\u003E columns, \u003Ccode\u003EK-101\u003C/code\u003E compressors). Type another to use it.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EInstruments\u003C/strong\u003E ask for letters (\u003Ccode\u003EFIC\u003C/code\u003E) and take the next loop number (\u003Ccode\u003EFIC-101\u003C/code\u003E), or you type the whole tag. The first letter says what is measured, the letters after it what the instrument does with it: \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDLIST\u003C/code\u003E reads them out in words (\u003Ccode\u003EFlow: indicate, control\u003C/code\u003E). A transmitter and its controller share a loop number.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EHand valves and in-line items\u003C/strong\u003E are not asked; give them a tag afterwards with \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDTAG\u003C/code\u003E: click the symbol, type its tag and a description. \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EA\u003C/span\u003E in \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDTAG\u003C/code\u003E tags every untagged piece of equipment at once, numbered from left to right.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOther facts about an item (service, design pressure and temperature, capacity, material, notes) go in \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EProperties\u003C/span\u003E, and come out in the equipment list.\u003C/p\u003E","text":"The library PIDSYMBOL places any of 52 symbols in five kinds, and a valve can carry any of five actuators. Kind Symbols Standard idea it follows Valves gate, globe, ball, check, butterfly, plug, needle, diaphragm, angle, three-way, pressure relief, rupture disc ISO 10628 (symbols for chemical and process engineering diagrams) Actuators diaphragm, motor, solenoid, piston, hand operated ISO 10628 Equipment vertical and horizontal vessel, storage tank, sphere, column, reactor, shell and tube and plate exchanger, air cooler, fired heater, centrifugal and positive displacement pump, compressor, fan, filter, agitator ISO 10628 Instruments balloons: field, main panel, local panel, shared display, computer function, programmable logic controller ISA-5.1 (instrument identification: the balloon and where it is mounted) In-line items reducer, cap, flange, blind flange, spectacle blind, union, orifice plate, strainer, sight glass, expansion joint, flame arrestor, specification break ISO 10628; orifice plate ISA-5.1; specification break ISO 14617 Connectors and line ends off-page connector (to, from), flow arrow, vent, drain, tie-in point ISO 14617 (symbols for diagrams), ISO 10628 Every shape is drawn by CadCraft and dedicated to the public domain (CC0 1.0): use them anywhere. The standards give the idea of a shape (a bow tie for a valve, a circle for a pump, a circle for an instrument); no vendor's symbol library and no standard's own artwork was copied or traced. The tables of letters and shapes in a standard are the standard's: for a drawing that has to follow one, check it against the standard itself. Placing symbols Type PIDSYMBOL. S chooses the symbol (its kind first), A turns the next symbols, and for a valve T chooses its actuator. Click to place; Enter ends. Nozzles. Equipment, valves and instruments have connection points (a pump's suction and discharge, a vessel's top, bottom and sides). A click near a line end or another symbol's connection puts the new symbol's nearest connection exactly there. In-line items cut the line. A valve, reducer, strainer or other in-line symbol clicked on a process line is turned along the line and cuts it: two pieces, each ending on the symbol. They keep the line number; one piece writes it. UNDO puts the line back whole. Valves with actuators have one more connection, on top of the actuator, where a signal line ends. A check valve, relief valve and rupture disc take no actuator. Tags Equipment, instruments and pressure relief devices need a tag; the checks say so when one is missing. Equipment is offered the next free tag with a prefix by kind (P-101 pumps, T-101 tanks and spheres, V-101 vessels, E-101 exchangers, C-101 columns, K-101 compressors). Type another to use it. Instruments ask for letters (FIC) and take the next loop number (FIC-101), or you type the whole tag. The first letter says what is measured, the letters after it what the instrument does with it: PIDLIST reads them out in words (Flow: indicate, control). A transmitter and its controller share a loop number. Hand valves and in-line items are not asked; give them a tag afterwards with PIDTAG: click the symbol, type its tag and a description. A in PIDTAG tags every untagged piece of equipment at once, numbered from left to right. Other facts about an item (service, design pressure and temperature, capacity, material, notes) go in Properties, and come out in the equipment list."},{"slug":"pid-lines","scope":"addon:pid","title":"P&ID: lines and line numbers","summary":"Process lines and the four kinds of signal line, how a line number is built, and keeping one number across valves and branches.","section":"tasks","order":20,"keywords":["line","process line","line number","signal","pneumatic","electric","software","capillary","service","spec","size","sequence","arrow","branch"],"headings":[{"id":"drawing-a-line","text":"Drawing a line","level":2},{"id":"the-line-number","text":"The line number","level":2},{"id":"valves-pieces-and-branches","text":"Valves, pieces and branches","level":2}],"html":"\u003Ch2 id=\"drawing-a-line\"\u003EDrawing a line\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EType \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDLINE\u003C/code\u003E and click the corners; Enter ends. Before the first point, \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EY\u003C/span\u003E chooses the kind of line, \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EV\u003C/span\u003E, \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EZ\u003C/span\u003E and \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EP\u003C/span\u003E the service, size and spec of a process line, \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EA\u003C/span\u003E the flow arrow, and \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EM\u003C/span\u003E copies the fields of a line you click. A line always starts as a process line; the service, size, spec and arrow are remembered for the next one.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA click near a nozzle, a line end or another line lands on it exactly, so what you draw is connected. A line started on the end of another process line carries on with its number.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"ht-wrap\"\u003E\u003Ctable class=\"ht\"\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003EKind\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003ELooks like\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003EMeans\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EProcess line\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eheavy continuous line\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Epipe: carries a line number\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EPneumatic signal\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ethin line with slashes across it\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eair signal\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EElectric signal\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Edashed\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eelectric signal\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ESoftware or data link\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Edotted\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Elink between control functions\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ECapillary tube\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Edash and dot\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Efilled sensing line\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/tbody\u003E\u003C/table\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe signal kinds follow the ideas of ISA-5.1; the drawing is CadCraft&#039;s own.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"the-line-number\"\u003EThe line number\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA process line&#039;s number is built from its fields by a scheme: size, service, sequence and spec joined by dashes (\u003Ccode\u003E2&quot;-PW-101-A1A\u003C/code\u003E). A line given a service gets the next free sequence number in that service, from 101. Change the scheme in \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESettings\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ECadCraft\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EP&amp;ID\u003C/span\u003E: put the parts in braces, in any order (\u003Ccode\u003E{svc}{seq}/{size}\u003C/code\u003E makes \u003Ccode\u003EPW101/2&quot;\u003C/code\u003E). Or type the number yourself in \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EProperties\u003C/span\u003E, in \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ELine number (typed)\u003C/span\u003E: it is used as typed.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDLN\u003C/code\u003E sets the service, size and spec of the lines you click; \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EN\u003C/span\u003E gives each a new number.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"valves-pieces-and-branches\"\u003EValves, pieces and branches\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA line cut by valves is several pieces with one number. The longest piece writes it (\u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EWrite the number on this piece\u003C/span\u003E in \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EProperties\u003C/span\u003E moves it). The line list counts the pieces as one line, from the first end to the last.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA line that ends on the middle of another line is a branch: the main&#039;s row in the line list names it. A line whose number changes where nothing sits between the two is flagged by \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDCHECK\u003C/code\u003E: put a reducer or a specification break there. A number may change at a valve.\u003C/p\u003E","text":"Drawing a line Type PIDLINE and click the corners; Enter ends. Before the first point, Y chooses the kind of line, V, Z and P the service, size and spec of a process line, A the flow arrow, and M copies the fields of a line you click. A line always starts as a process line; the service, size, spec and arrow are remembered for the next one. A click near a nozzle, a line end or another line lands on it exactly, so what you draw is connected. A line started on the end of another process line carries on with its number. Kind Looks like Means Process line heavy continuous line pipe: carries a line number Pneumatic signal thin line with slashes across it air signal Electric signal dashed electric signal Software or data link dotted link between control functions Capillary tube dash and dot filled sensing line The signal kinds follow the ideas of ISA-5.1; the drawing is CadCraft's own. The line number A process line's number is built from its fields by a scheme: size, service, sequence and spec joined by dashes (2\"-PW-101-A1A). A line given a service gets the next free sequence number in that service, from 101. Change the scheme in Settings › CadCraft › P&ID: put the parts in braces, in any order ({svc}{seq}/{size} makes PW101/2\"). Or type the number yourself in Properties, in Line number (typed): it is used as typed. PIDLN sets the service, size and spec of the lines you click; N gives each a new number. Valves, pieces and branches A line cut by valves is several pieces with one number. The longest piece writes it (Write the number on this piece in Properties moves it). The line list counts the pieces as one line, from the first end to the last. A line that ends on the middle of another line is a branch: the main's row in the line list names it. A line whose number changes where nothing sits between the two is flagged by PIDCHECK: put a reducer or a specification break there. A number may change at a valve."},{"slug":"pid-lists","scope":"addon:pid","title":"P&ID: lists on the sheet, CSV and XLSX","summary":"The line list, equipment list, instrument index and valve list: on the sheet as tables that stay current, and out as one workbook or a CSV.","section":"tasks","order":30,"keywords":["list","line list","equipment list","instrument index","valve list","table","export","csv","xlsx","spreadsheet"],"headings":[{"id":"the-four-lists","text":"The four lists","level":2},{"id":"on-the-sheet","text":"On the sheet","level":2},{"id":"out-as-a-file","text":"Out as a file","level":2}],"html":"\u003Ch2 id=\"the-four-lists\"\u003EThe four lists\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"ht-wrap\"\u003E\u003Ctable class=\"ht\"\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003EList\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003EOne row per\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003EColumns\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ELine list\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eline number\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Esize, service, spec, insulation, from, to, branches\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EEquipment list\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Epiece of equipment\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Etag, type, description, service, design pressure, design temperature, capacity, material, nozzles used, connected lines, notes\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EInstrument index\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Einstrument\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Etag, function in words, loop, mounting, service, description, what it is connected to\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EValve list\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Evalve and tagged in-line item\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Etag, type, actuator, line, service, description, notes\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/tbody\u003E\u003C/table\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EFrom and To follow the line through valves and in-line items to the equipment, instrument or connector at each end (\u003Ccode\u003ET-101 (right)\u003C/code\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003EP-101 (suction)\u003C/code\u003E); an end that joins nothing says so.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"on-the-sheet\"\u003EOn the sheet\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EType \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDLIST\u003C/code\u003E, choose a list and click the table&#039;s top-left corner. The table is an object: it follows the drawing, so tagging a pump, drawing a line or erasing a valve changes its rows in the same undo step. Text height is in \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESettings\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ECadCraft\u003C/span\u003E › \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EP&amp;ID\u003C/span\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"out-as-a-file\"\u003EOut as a file\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EType \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EEXPORT\u003C/code\u003E and choose \u003Cstrong\u003EP&amp;ID lists (XLSX workbook)\u003C/strong\u003E: one worksheet per list, a bold header row, text throughout. Or \u003Cstrong\u003EP&amp;ID lists (CSV)\u003C/strong\u003E: every list in one file, each under its name. A cell that starts with \u003Ccode\u003E=\u003C/code\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003E+\u003C/code\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003E-\u003C/code\u003E or \u003Ccode\u003E@\u003C/code\u003E is written as text, never as a formula.\u003C/p\u003E","text":"The four lists List One row per Columns Line list line number size, service, spec, insulation, from, to, branches Equipment list piece of equipment tag, type, description, service, design pressure, design temperature, capacity, material, nozzles used, connected lines, notes Instrument index instrument tag, function in words, loop, mounting, service, description, what it is connected to Valve list valve and tagged in-line item tag, type, actuator, line, service, description, notes From and To follow the line through valves and in-line items to the equipment, instrument or connector at each end (T-101 (right), P-101 (suction)); an end that joins nothing says so. On the sheet Type PIDLIST, choose a list and click the table's top-left corner. The table is an object: it follows the drawing, so tagging a pump, drawing a line or erasing a valve changes its rows in the same undo step. Text height is in Settings › CadCraft › P&ID. Out as a file Type EXPORT and choose P&ID lists (XLSX workbook): one worksheet per list, a bold header row, text throughout. Or P&ID lists (CSV): every list in one file, each under its name. A cell that starts with =, +, - or @ is written as text, never as a formula."},{"slug":"pid-checks","scope":"addon:pid","title":"Check a P&ID","summary":"Find untagged items, duplicate tags, open line ends and more, and go to each one.","section":"tasks","order":40,"keywords":["pidcheck","check","error","warning","untagged","duplicate tag","open end","line number","loop","instrument"],"headings":[],"html":"\u003Cp\u003EType \u003Ccode class=\"hcmd\"\u003EPIDCHECK\u003C/code\u003E (\u003Ccode\u003EPIDC\u003C/code\u003E). The history lists every finding, errors first. Type a finding&#039;s number to zoom to it and select what it names; press \u003Ckbd class=\"hk\"\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"k-mac\" title=\"Return\"\u003EReturn\u003C/span\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"k-pc\"\u003EEnter\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/kbd\u003E to end.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cdiv class=\"ht-wrap\"\u003E\u003Ctable class=\"ht\"\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003EFinding\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003ELevel\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\"col\"\u003EMeans\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ENo tag\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eerror\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eequipment, an instrument or a relief device has no tag\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EDuplicate tag\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eerror\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Etwo items have one tag (case does not count; off-page connectors may repeat)\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EOpen end\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Eerror\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ea line end joins nothing\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EOpen port\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ewarning\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ea valve or in-line item is joined on one side only\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ENo line number\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ewarning\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ea process line has no number\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ENo loop number\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ewarning\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ean instrument tag has letters but no number\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ENumber changes\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ewarning\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Etwo lines of different numbers meet end to end with nothing between them\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EInstrument alone\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ewarning\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003Ean instrument has no line attached\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/tbody\u003E\u003C/table\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe checks are a drafting aid: a clean result means the drawing is consistent with itself, not that the plant is right.\u003C/p\u003E","text":"Type PIDCHECK (PIDC). The history lists every finding, errors first. Type a finding's number to zoom to it and select what it names; press Enter to end. Finding Level Means No tag error equipment, an instrument or a relief device has no tag Duplicate tag error two items have one tag (case does not count; off-page connectors may repeat) Open end error a line end joins nothing Open port warning a valve or in-line item is joined on one side only No line number warning a process line has no number No loop number warning an instrument tag has letters but no number Number changes warning two lines of different numbers meet end to end with nothing between them Instrument alone warning an instrument has no line attached The checks are a drafting aid: a clean result means the drawing is consistent with itself, not that the plant is right."},{"slug":"pid-not-built-yet","scope":"addon:pid","title":"P&ID: not built yet","summary":"What the P&ID add-on does not do yet, so you know before you plan a job around it.","section":"reference","order":90,"keywords":["limits","not built","missing","roadmap","p&id"],"headings":[{"id":"not-built-yet","text":"Not built yet","level":2}],"html":"\u003Ch2 id=\"not-built-yet\"\u003ENot built yet\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ESpecifications and sizes from a pipe spec\u003C/strong\u003E: a line number&#039;s size and spec are text; nothing checks them against a piping class. The 3D piping with specs is a separate add-on in BimCraft.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ELoop diagrams, cause-and-effect and data sheets\u003C/strong\u003E from the instrument index.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ESeveral sheets with a drawing list\u003C/strong\u003E and cross-references between off-page connectors: the connectors carry a label; nothing joins them across drawings yet.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EBubbles for sub-systems, insulation and heat tracing marks\u003C/strong\u003E: insulation is a text field in the line list.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EMoving a line when an item it ends on moves\u003C/strong\u003E: lines are never attached. Move the line&#039;s end with its grip.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ESymbols from other libraries\u003C/strong\u003E: the library is CadCraft&#039;s own; draw others as blocks.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EOther languages\u003C/strong\u003E for the add-on&#039;s words: they come with the next language update.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E","text":"Not built yet Specifications and sizes from a pipe spec: a line number's size and spec are text; nothing checks them against a piping class. The 3D piping with specs is a separate add-on in BimCraft. Loop diagrams, cause-and-effect and data sheets from the instrument index. Several sheets with a drawing list and cross-references between off-page connectors: the connectors carry a label; nothing joins them across drawings yet. Bubbles for sub-systems, insulation and heat tracing marks: insulation is a text field in the line list. Moving a line when an item it ends on moves: lines are never attached. Move the line's end with its grip. Symbols from other libraries: the library is CadCraft's own; draw others as blocks. Other languages for the add-on's words: they come with the next language update."}]};
